(Plan 291 Finding 6: `but if` conditional branches for `print` parse their
own `without newline`, independent of the base statement's. A following
marker print (with its own trailing newline) makes it visible in the
captured output whether a newline snuck in after the conditional branch.)

a number called v1 is 1.
Print "." without newline, but if v1 is equal to 1 print "#" without newline.
Print "|".

a number called v2 is 2.
Print "." without newline, but if v2 is equal to 1 print "#" without newline.
Print "|".
